            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "I don’t have live news access, so I can’t verify today’s very latest Perseverance update. As of my latest reliable information:\n\n- NASA’s Perseverance rover was still operating in Jezero Crater, exploring ancient river and lakebed environments that may once have been habitable.\n- The rover had collected and sealed multiple rock-core samples for possible return to Earth by a future Mars Sample Return mission.\n- Perseverance was investigating sedimentary rocks, carbonates, and other minerals that could preserve signs of ancient microbial life if it ever existed on Mars.\n- The Ingenuity helicopter, which traveled with Perseverance, ended its flight mission in early 2024 after rotor damage, but it greatly exceeded expectations with dozens of flights.\n- NASA was reassessing the Mars Sample Return program because of cost and schedule concerns, while still emphasizing the scientific value of Perseverance’s cached samples.\n\nFor the actual latest news, the best sources are NASA’s Mars 2020/Perseverance mission page or NASA/JPL press releases.",
